  "body": "**[Original report](https://bitbucket.org/agriggio/art/issues/38) by Paul Matthijsse (Bitbucket: [Paul Matthijsse](https://bitbucket.org/Paul Matthijsse), ).**\n\n----------------------------------------\n\nHello, I propose to re-arrange the order in which masks are shown, on top of the Color Correction panel. By default there is always a slider visible, that hides the most important part of this window: the name of the mask and the checkmarks. I think a photographer is less interested in those numbers and more interested in the mask name and if it is activated or not. See attached file, I had to expand the right panel a lot.\n\nSo mask name left, then the power button, then the numbers.\n\nAnd tooltips would be welcome here as well, for those icons on the right \\(copy, new, delete…\\).\n",
